  "scope": "No-fault sequential integer-epoch Java controller, uniform HCA002 and observation-only profile004.",
  "proof": [
    "Wrapper records every new task generated at epoch before invoking controller at the same epoch.",
    "Controller appends all new tasks to unfinished planning list, snapshots the full count, and removes exactly that many heads; failure appends to tail while remaining tasks still execute.",
    "Consequently each newly generated task is attempted exactly once in that epoch. release_epoch equals first planning attempt, regardless of later successful admission.",
    "Source taskList entries blocked by pending same-source tasks have not yet joined unfinished planning list; their time is separate preplanning source hold.",
    "outputstarttime fourth column is written only on path success; third column is default-zero pass_time after reading new-task four-field epoch records, not canonical release."
  ],
  "source_model": [
    "Stable original nominal pass_time order, preserving raw input row order for equal keys. Ceil is a release gate, not the sorting key.",
    "An unavailable EBS head masks the whole source queue, blocking later ready bags.",
    "Every source generates at most one task per integer epoch. A pending unsuccessful source task prevents generating the next. Generation precedes controller success, so success at e allows next head no earlier than e+1.",
    "Although generation precedes goal report processing, causal mask predicts the report from saved route.size()==2 and epoch>=goal.t1, allowing outbound at that same epoch."
  ],
